          "SPEC (Latin specere, to look) means look.",
          "VIDE, and in its past form VIS (Latin",
          "videre, visus, to see), means see.",
          "",
          "  inspect     into + look",
          "  prospect    forward + look",
          "  provide     ahead + see",
          "  revise      again + see",
          "",
          "From here the root shifts its vowel. SPEC",
          "becomes SPIC in conspicuous and suspicion.",
          "The word is the same; the spelling bends",
          "to the ending.",
          "",
          "A visa is a document that has been seen:",
          "carta visa, a paper inspected.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 18 CARDS: spec and vide words."
