    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "FRACT, also FRAG and FRING (Latin",
          "frangere, fractus, to break), means break.",
          "RUPT (Latin rumpere, ruptus) means break",
          "or burst.",
          "",
          "  fracture    a breaking",
          "  fragment    a broken piece",
          "  erupt       out + break",
          "  interrupt   between + break",
          "",
          "Two roots, one idea: frangere breaks a",
          "thing, rumpere bursts it open.",
          "",
          "Bankrupt came through Italian banca rotta,",
          "a broken bench: the money changer's table",
          "was said to be broken when he failed.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 16 CARDS: fract and rupt words."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 8"
      }
