    "trigger_card_number": 169,
    "title": "LESSON 9: STEP AND GO",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "GRAD, and in its other form GRESS (Latin",
          "gradi, gressus, to step), means step.",
          "CEDE, also CEED and CESS (Latin cedere,",
          "cessus, to go, to yield), means go.",
          "",
          "  progress    forward + step",
          "  digress     aside + step",
          "  precede     before + go",
          "  recede      back + go",
          "",
          "A grade is a step and so is a degree: to",
          "degrade is to put down a step.",
          "",
          "Only three English words keep the -ceed",
          "spelling: exceed, proceed and succeed.",
          "The rest take -cede.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 17 CARDS: grad and cede words."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 9"
      }
    ]
  },
