    "title": "LESSON 10: PLACE AND HANG",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "PON, and in its other forms POS and POSIT",
          "(Latin ponere, positus, to place), means",
          "place. PEND, also PENS (Latin pendere,",
          "pensus, to hang), means hang.",
          "",
          "  compose     together + place",
          "  postpone    after + place",
          "  suspend     beneath + hang",
          "  append      onto + hang",
          "",
          "PEND also means weigh out. Money was",
          "weighed on a balance before it was",
          "counted, so expend, pension and",
          "compensate are all weighing words.",
          "",
          "A pendant hangs from the neck and a",
          "pending case hangs undecided.",
          "THE NEXT 19 CARDS: pon and pend words."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 10"
      }
    ]
  },
