          "vertere, versus, to turn), means turn.",
          "FLECT, also FLEX (Latin flectere, flexus,",
          "to bend), means bend.",
          "",
          "  convert     completely + turn",
          "  avert       away + turn",
          "  reflect     back + bend",
          "  inflexible  not + able to be bent",
          "",
          "The universe is everything turned into",
          "one; a controversy is two sides turned",
          "against each other.",
          "",
          "Versus is the same root, turned toward:",
          "the courts wrote it between two names,",
          "and sport copied the courts.",
